menu "RNG Analysis Configuration"

    config RNG_ENTROPY_MODE
        int "Entropy source mode (0–7)"
        default 0
        range 0 7
        help
            Selects which hardware entropy sources are initialised before
            collecting samples.

            0  BARE        - No entropy sources (RC oscillator only)
            1  WIFI        - WiFi RF subsystem (not connected)
            2  BT          - Bluetooth RF subsystem (BLE mode)
            3  WIFI_BT     - WiFi + Bluetooth RF
            4  ADC         - SAR ADC entropy path (bootloader_random_enable)
            5  ADC_WIFI    - SAR ADC + WiFi RF
            6  ADC_BT      - SAR ADC + Bluetooth RF
            7  ADC_WIFI_BT - All sources active (strongest)

    config RNG_NUM_SAMPLES
        int "Number of 32-bit samples to collect"
        default 250000
        range 1000 50000000
        help
            Total number of esp_random() calls per run.
            250 000 samples = 1 000 000 bytes = 8 000 000 bits.
            NIST SP 800-22 tests 7-15 need ≥1 Mbit.
            PractRand is meaningful from ~1 MB (250 000 samples) upward.

endmenu
